  "description": "McGuirk Beggan Property are delighted to present No. 42E Clarence Mangan Road to the market. Behind its attractive original red brick façade lies a wonderful and fully refurbished home that has been thoughtfully modernised while carefully retaining the charm and character synonymous with artisan dwellings of this era.\nOriginally built in the early 1900`s, this turnkey residence underwent a comprehensive refurbishment in 2013 including rewiring, replumbing, replastering, new concrete floor and insulation works, creating a warm, comfortable and highly efficient home without compromising its period appeal. The property offers a superb balance of old and new, with original features sitting effortlessly alongside tasteful modern finishes.\n\nThe living accommodation is bright, stylish and full of character throughout, with the front reception room beautifully showcasing the charm of the original artisan design. Featuring impressive high ceilings, wood effect flooring, a marble surround fireplace and a newly fitted sash window perfectly complementing the attractive red brick façade, this space offers a warm and elegant atmosphere. To the rear, a modern fully fitted kitchen is finished with tiled flooring and splashback and provides direct access to a private rear yard area. The generous double bedroom benefits from fitted wardrobes and a bespoke fitted vanity unit, while a separate washroom leads through to the contemporary shower room, completing the well-designed accommodation.\n\nClarence Mangan Road enjoys an exceptionally convenient city centre location in the heart of Dublin 8, one of Dublin`s most vibrant and sought-after residential districts. The property is within walking distance of a host of city amenities including St. Stephen`s Green (approx. 2km) and Christchurch Cathedral (approx. 1.5km), while Grafton Street, Camden Street, Temple Bar and The Liberties are all easily accessible on foot. Residents are spoiled with an abundance of cafés, restaurants, shops and cultural attractions nearby. The area is also extremely well serviced by public transport including numerous Dublin Bus routes together with the nearby LUAS Red Line.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a charming artisan home rich in character yet presented in true turnkey condition in one of Dublin city`s most desirable and historic locations. Early viewing is highly recommended.\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only.",
